-- title:
--   Unfolded Rankin–Selberg S-part as a torus integral
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a number field, and let $\alpha$ be the monoid homomorphism from the idèles $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ to $\mathbb{R}^\times$ obtained from the distributive Haar character of $\mathbb{A}_K$ (so $\alpha(t)$ is the idèle norm $\|t\|$), assumed pointwise positive via $h\alpha$. Fix $c\in[0,\infty]$ satisfying the Iwasawa disintegration hypothesis: for every measurable fundamental domain $D$ for the principal idèles $K^\times$ in $(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times$ with respect to idèlic Haar measure, and every measurable $f:\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)\to[0,\infty]$ invariant under left multiplication by the subgroup generated by the rational central scalars and the full adelic unipotent group, $\int f\,$ over the quotient measure equals $c\int_D\int_{(\mathbb{A}_K)^\times}\int_{\mathbf{K}} f(z\,\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)\,\|t\|^{-1}\,dk\,d^\times t\,d^\times z$, where $\mathbf{K}$ is the adelic maximal compact subgroup with its Haar measure. Fix a finite set $S$ of primes of $\mathcal{O}_K$, such a measurable fundamental domain $D$, reals $0<e_1<e_2$, and $C\in[0,\infty]$ with $\mathrm{vol}(D\cap\{z:\|z\|^2 r\in[e_1,e_2]\})=C$ for every $r>0$. Fix further data $D_0$, $U$, $gen$ assembling, together with the adelic box, the carrier pins used for the Whittaker coefficient (whose adelic measure is the additive Haar measure conditioned on the box); a global additive character $\psi$ of $\mathbb{A}_K$ trivial on $K$, continuous and non-trivial; idèle characters $\mu,\nu,\omega_x,\omega_y$ with values in $\mathbb{C}^\times$, a real $w$, with $\mu,\nu$ unitary and $\omega_x(z)\overline{\omega_y(z)}\mu(z)\nu(z)=\|z\|^{2w}$ for all $z$; continuous functions $x,y$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ invariant under left multiplication by the global points $\mathrm{GL}_2(K)$ and transforming under the central scalars by $\omega_x$, $\omega_y$; and $s\in\mathbb{C}$ together with a continuous $\varphi$ which is an induced section for the characters $\mu\cdot\alpha^{s+1/2}$ and $\nu\cdot\alpha^{-(s+1/2)}$, that is, $\varphi(bg)=\mu\alpha^{s+1/2}(b_{00})\,\nu\alpha^{-(s+1/2)}(b_{11})\varphi(g)$ for $b$ in the adelic Borel subgroup. Then two assertions hold. First, an identity in $[0,\infty]$: the lower integral, over the set of classes in the quotient of $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_K)$ by rational centre and adelic unipotent whose chosen representative satisfies, at every prime $v\notin S$, $v(\det g)=\max(v(g_{10}),v(g_{11}))^2$, of the extended norm of the integrand $\mathbf{1}_{\{\|\det g\|\in[e_1,e_2]\}}(g)\,W_1(x)(g)\overline{W_1(y)(g)}\varphi(g)\|\det g\|^{-w}$ evaluated at that representative, equals $c\,C\int\!\!\int \|W_1(x)(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)\overline{W_1(y)(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)}\varphi(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)\|\,\|t\|^{-w-1}\,dk\,d\nu_S(t)$, where $W_1$ denotes the first Whittaker coefficient for $\psi$ and the given pins, and $\nu_S$ is the $S$-part measure, the image under the projection $\mathrm{partAt}$ of idèlic Haar measure restricted to the idèles that are units outside $S$. Second, if that double lower integral is finite, then the corresponding Bochner integral, namely $\mathrm{sPartIntegral}$ for $S$, the pins, $\psi$, $x$, $y$, $\varphi$, $w$, $e_1$, $e_2$, equals $c\,C$ (real parts of the extended reals, viewed in $\mathbb{C}$) times $\int\!\!\int W_1(x)(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)\overline{W_1(y)(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)}\varphi(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)\,\|t\|^{-w-1}\,dk\,d\nu_S(t)$.
--
--   This is the evaluation, by Iwasawa decomposition, of the $S\cup\infty$ part of the unfolded Rankin–Selberg integral for $\mathrm{GL}_2\times\mathrm{GL}_2$: the central variable enters only through the norm slab indicator, whose volume over the fundamental domain is the constant $C$, leaving a torus-times-compact integral of the product of two Whittaker coefficients against the induced section. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.RankinSelberg.analyticOnNhd_sPartIntegral_and_pos_of_shell_surgery`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.RankinSelberg.analyticOnNhd_sPartIntegral_and_pos_of_shell_surgery) and [`AutomorphicForm.RankinSelberg.analyticOnNhd_sPartIntegral_pair_and_ne_zero_of_ball_surgery`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.RankinSelberg.analyticOnNhd_sPartIntegral_pair_and_ne_zero_of_ball_surgery), where analyticity in $s$ and non-vanishing of the $S$-part are derived.
